35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The minutes show that the covered spots have been held by the same flats for five years without any review. It seems the current arrangement has just been left as is, which might be causing some underlying tension.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is quite a long time for things to remain unchanged, Misaki-san. I noticed that some spots stay dry while others are quite wet, and it seems some neighbors have to move other bikes just to leave.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, it looks like our ""system"" is basically non-existent! I found out the building account is practically empty—just cleaning and lights. If we want any real improvements, we'll have to ask everyone for more money.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"The handover file indicates that the treasurer already spends three hours a month on basic collections. Adding a complex per-space billing system would only increase that burden, which we must avoid.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that some daily riders are actually willing to pay extra to get a spot! Also, the complaint log is full of people annoyed by bikes leaning on each other, but nobody knows who to blame!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, it's interesting that some are willing to pay. However, if we only prioritize those who can pay, we might create a divide between neighbors. We should be careful not to let money ruin the atmosphere.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Misaki-san. Kindness and harmony are more precious than money. It makes me sad to think of neighbors feeling frustrated because their bikes are leaning or getting wet in the rain. We should find a gentle way to solve this.,"{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, @Shizue, you're both so sweet, but let's be real! If people are willing to pay, why not use that to actually fund the building? We can't just rely on ""harmony"" to fix a leaky roof!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May, while funding is necessary, we must be realistic about the labor. If we implement a payment system for spots, who will manage the billing and collection? We cannot simply add more work to the treasurer's plate.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, maybe we can make it super simple so it's not a chore! But @Misaki, if the same people have had the best spots for five years, isn't that already unfair? We should definitely shake things up!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, it is unfair, but a sudden, drastic change could create new conflicts. We need a transition that doesn't make people resent each other. Let's find a balance between fairness and maintaining our current peace.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki-san, you are so thoughtful. Perhaps we could consider a rotation? That way, everyone gets a turn in the dry spots, and no one feels left out or burdened by the rain. It would be a very kind way to share.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"Rotation sounds a bit tedious, doesn't it? Who's going to manage the schedule? I still think we should look at a fee. It solves the funding issue and the fairness problem in one go!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, that is exactly my point. A rotation schedule or a fee system both require constant administration. We must ensure that whatever we decide doesn't become another abandoned task because it was too much work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, I get that, but doing nothing is also a problem! If we just leave it, people will keep grumbling. Maybe we can use a simple lottery once a year? That's way less work than a monthly schedule!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"A lottery once a year is a reasonable compromise. It's fair, requires minimal effort, and prevents the same people from holding the best spots indefinitely without creating a complex payment system that could cause friction.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"A lottery sounds like a lovely idea, Mio-san. It gives everyone an equal chance and keeps things lighthearted. I only hope we can also find a way to stop the bikes from leaning on each other.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"A lottery is fine for the spots, but I'm still not giving up on the money! If we're shaking things up, let's at least charge a small fee to build up our empty accounts. Who's with me?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"@May, I must disagree. Adding a fee requires monthly tracking and collection, which we've already seen is a burden. Let's prioritize a simple, sustainable system like the lottery over a complex financial one.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@May, I love your energy, but @George is right about the work! Let's stick to the lottery for now to keep it simple and fair. We can figure out the money part later!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
