60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Looking at the options, Option C seems the most stable. It addresses the unfairness of the last five years without introducing the financial friction or administrative burden that Options A and B might bring.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Misaki-san. Option C is a very gentle way to ensure everyone is treated equally. It feels like a fair and peaceful solution that would make all our neighbors smile.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Ugh, you're all so boring! Option A is the only one that actually helps the building's bank account. Why are we so afraid of a little paperwork if it means we actually have money for repairs?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"@May, it is not about being afraid, but about being practical. We have already seen that the treasurer is stretched thin. Option C is sustainable; Option A is a recipe for burnout and eventual failure.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm with George and Misaki-san! Option C is the most exciting because it's like a game, and it totally fixes the problem of the same people always getting the best spots. Let's go with the lottery!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I understand your concern for the building's funds, but we must prioritize the residents' relationships. A payment system could make neighbors view each other as competitors rather than community members. Option C maintains the peace.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May-san, your heart is in the right place wanting to help the building, but perhaps we can find another way to save money. Let us choose a path that keeps everyone's hearts light and happy.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, my heart is in the right place, but my eyes are on the empty ledger! If we just ""hope"" for money, we'll be staring at a leaky roof while we're all being ""light and happy."" Option A is the only adult choice here!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, being an adult means recognizing the limits of our resources, including time. A system that fails because it is too tedious to manage is not a professional choice; it is a mistake. Option C is the only sustainable path.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@May, you're so funny, but we can't let the building go broke just to make things complicated! Option C is fair, fast, and easy. Let's just do the lottery and keep everyone happy!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I believe the risk of creating a divided atmosphere is a higher cost than a lack of funds. Option B would be too chaotic, and Option A too divisive. Option C is the most balanced choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May-san, please do not be too discouraged. We can always discuss a separate, simple way to contribute to the building's funds later. For now, let us choose the lottery to bring everyone together in harmony.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, you're too sweet for your own good! Fine, if you're all determined to stay broke and ""harmonious,"" I'll stop fighting. But don't come crying to me when the ceiling starts leaking! I'll vote for C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,I am glad we have reached a consensus. Option C is the only choice that ensures the system will actually be maintained without overburdening any single resident. I will cast my vote for the annual lottery.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"Yay! I'm so glad we all agree! Option C is definitely the way to go. It's fair, it's simple, and it'll stop all that grumbling. I'm voting for the annual lottery!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I am glad we could reach an agreement that prioritizes the community's well-being. I will also vote for Option C, the Annual Lottery, to ensure a fair and peaceful environment for everyone.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It warms my heart to see us all in agreement. I shall also vote for Option C, the Annual Lottery. Let us move forward with kindness and a smile for all our neighbors.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"I'll go along with the crowd! I'm voting for Option C, the Annual Lottery. Just remember, I warned you about the budget! Now, who's treating me to a drink for being so flexible?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,"I will also vote for Option C, the Annual Lottery. It is the most practical and sustainable solution for our building. I believe this decision will serve us well without creating unnecessary burdens.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm voting for Option C, the Annual Lottery too! I'm so happy we figured this out together. Now let's make it happen and get everyone smiling again!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
